     "text": "{\"count\":4,\"rationale\":\"The target is an OR over codeRepo, dbReplica, mailArchive and vaultRead, so all four must be cut. There are four attack paths that share no blockable step: (1) phishing → configSecret → backupHost → mailArchive; (2) wifiGuest/vpnGateway → sshKey + mailClient → dbLogin → printServer → vaultRead; (3) wifiGuest → containerHost → memoryDump → monitoringHost → dbReplica; (4) iotDevice + kerberoast → apiToken → jumpHost → codeRepo. Because these paths are disjoint, at least 4 blocks are needed. Blocking just the four collection steps (codeRepo, dbReplica, mailArchive, vaultRead) cuts every route to the target, so 4 is also enough.\"}"
    }
